<p>The United States has completed the handover of military bases in Syria to the Syrian government, ending a formal U.S. troop presence that had lasted for years and included the Qasrak air base in northeastern Hasakah province. Syrian officials said the transfer happened in full coordination with Washington. Syrian authorities cast the handover as a sign that the state can now lead counterterrorism operations from within the country. They also linked it to the integration of the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces into national structures after a ceasefire deal announced in January. The U.S. intervened in Syria in 2014 to fight Islamic State, and recent reporting says American troops first arrived in 2015.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oNZnDDn1c0cJprZT0Fqd9y7VUdD4vECPToLRv3KawNM-c-1P_x4Vef0egDLA6V51o6Yp4MPiDZNRP8C1jqEIKg--a5Z9Iw-0VRbnGCPJ5tsq' alt='Syrian youth look on as a convoy of military equipment is transported along the Damascus–Amman highway following completion of the US withdrawal.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Regional reach: In recent months, Syria&#x27;s government has expanded its control into parts of the northeast that had previously been held by U.S.-allied Kurdish forces.</li><li>Damascus&#x27;s argument: Syria&#x27;s foreign ministry said the circumstances once used to justify a U.S. military presence on Syrian territory had fundamentally changed.</li><li>Previous alignment: The Kurdish fighters covered by the January integration framework had long been allied with the United States before moving into Syrian state structures.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Syrian government: Syria&#x27;s foreign ministry welcomed the completed handover and said it happened in full coordination between the Syrian and American governments. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992437/syria-completes-takeover-of-military-sites-used-by-us-forces'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>U.S. Central Command: CENTCOM described the move as a deliberate, conditions-based transition while stressing that support for partner-led anti-IS operations would continue. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992437/syria-completes-takeover-of-military-sites-used-by-us-forces'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/syria-says-takes-over-northeast-base-after-international-coalition-pullout/article70870894.ece'>Syria says takes over northeast base after international coalition pullout</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/16/world/middleeast/us-handover-military-bases-syria.html'>U.S. Completes Handover of Military Bases in Syria</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992437/syria-completes-takeover-of-military-sites-used-by-us-forces'>Syria completes takeover of military sites used by US forces</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/us-military-fully-withdraws-syria-after-10-years'>U.S. troops complete their withdrawal from the Qasrak air base in Hasakah province, ending U.S. involvement in Syria after troops first arrived in 2015 to fight against the Islamic State. (Middle East Eye)</a> - middleeasteye.net</li></ul>